     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>1. the p value that appears in the $naive corresponds to the corrected (scaled) p value? (this p value is the scaled difference between the naive chi square p values?) </div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>No, naïve means unscaled (so pretending the data were normal), not robust.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
